	(text "f_C is upper bounded by the lower of 1/10 f_SW and 1/5 f_RHPZ.\n\nR_COUT is the ESR of C2, C3, C4, C5, and C6.\nThe datasheet states C7 can be left open if it's below 10 pF.\nIf R_COUT is less than 0.165 mOhms, C7 can be left open.\n\nEN/UVLO: Programmable undervoltage lockout.\nLogic high enables (>1.15V) & logic low turns it into shutdown mode. Can be used \nfor undervoltage lockout. \n\nPG: Power good. \nWhen VOUT > 95% of the setting output voltage, high impedance.\nWhen VOUT < 90% of the setting output voltage, low level.\n\nCC: When IOUT limit is triggered, low level.\n\nEXTVCC: When logic high or floating, internal LDO. \nWhen logic low, external 5V LDO.\n\nDITH/SYNC: Use a capacitor to ground to set the dithering frequency.\nWhen short to ground or pulled above 1.2V, no dithering.\nAn external clock can be applied to sychronize the switching frequency.\n\nMODE: When logic high, forced PWM mode. When logic low, auto PFM mode.\nCan NOT be floating in application."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.165 140.335 0)
